---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "./_support/support.scss";
---

<BaseLayout title="Support" pageTitle="Crona support" description="Get help with Crona through the docs, GitHub issues, and release list.">
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="page-header flow measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
      <h1>Support for Crona</h1>
      <p>
        The fastest path to help is usually the docs first, then GitHub if you need to report a bug or check a recent
        change.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="support-grid page-body">
      <a class="support-card" href="/docs/">
        <span>Docs</span>
        <strong>Open the documentation</strong>
        <p>Start with setup, daily workflows, exports, alerts, keymaps, and automation guides.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="support-card" href="/docs/install/">
        <span>Setup help</span>
        <strong>Check install and runtime docs</strong>
        <p>Use this for platform setup, shell completions, notifications, renderer notes, and update basics.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="support-card external-card" href="https://github.com/webxsid/crona/issues" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Bug reports</span>
        <strong>Open GitHub issues</strong>
        <p>Report reproducible bugs, missing behavior, or broken docs where the core project can track them.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="support-card" href="/changelog/">
        <span>Recent changes</span>
        <strong>Browse releases</strong>
        <p>Check the on-site release cards first, then jump to GitHub for the raw notes and artifacts.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
